{"kind":"request","text":"AD-1: application act admission reads the installation's current state and release, not its birth provenance. Per e9191a97: act-admission.ts:87-100 caches the birth provenance as immutable and never reads N's state. Outcome: (1) a scope whose installation N is replaced refuses new acts with application-replaced, so nothing is sealed after U2's archive stop; (2) after an in-place upgrade, admission checks N's current release against APPLICATION_TRUST, so retiring the birth release after an upgrade (ruling 1704aaca) leaves the scope working. Reds: an act in a replaced scope is admitted today; an act after in-place upgrade plus retirement of the birth release is refused as application-revoked today. Keep the admission cost near today's: a cached read that changes only when N's state or release changes is fine; one Rules read per act needs the numbers first.","body":{"conditions":"Builds on U2; full gate before review; state the added requests per admitted act and per room per hour (no new alarm or retry), and how the cache stays correct after an upgrade; U1, U2 and AD-1 deploy together","target_head":"7cb207e1035c966086ebae7a0d3b20a7997fc817","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}